    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Landscapes",
     "texto": [
      "**Fjord** is a narrow arm of the sea, often surrounded by mountains; **innsjø** is an inland lake. **Elv** is river and **dal**, valley.",
      "**Skog** means forest. In Bokmål, its definite forms are **skogen**, **elva**, **dalen** and **fjorden**; note that the article is attached to the end of the noun, unlike English «the», which comes before it."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
